# .gitignore tells Git which files/folders to NEVER track or commit — usually
# because they're auto-generated and can be recreated from source, or because
# they're specific to one person's machine/editor and shouldn't be shared.

target/       # Maven's build output folder (compiled classes, the packaged .jar) — regenerated every build, no need to store it in Git
*.class       # Compiled Java bytecode files — also just build output
.idea/        # IntelliJ IDEA's project settings folder — personal editor config, not project code
*.iml         # IntelliJ IDEA module files — same reason as above
.vscode/      # VS Code's workspace settings folder — personal editor config
HELP.md       # A default placeholder file Spring Initializr generates — not something we need to keep
